-- ===== aliasing and linearity =====
-- EXPECT: 'insert' takes 'a copyable dict str 'a copyable
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- a tagged box stays linear, so insert's guard still sees it
dict "k" 42 box 'x tag insert drop

-- EXPECT: 'drop' takes 'a copyable
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- the same laundering, one step earlier: dropping a tagged box leaked it
42 box 'x tag drop

-- EXPECT: 'dup' takes 'a copyable
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- and `dup` on one produced two references to a single BoxData
42 box 'x tag dup drop drop

-- EXPECT: 'push' takes 'a copyable list 'a copyable
-- EXPECT: int box is a box: it cannot be copied
-- a list is as stackable as a dict; push has to reject it for the same reason
list 42 box 'x tag push drop

